// HF17 / VIZ 4.3.0: how emergency consensus ENDS, and what schedule it ends on.
//
// Two changes, one fork, because they are the same moment in the chain's life:
//  1. The exit threshold stops being a constant (75% of CHAIN_MAX_VALIDATORS = 15) and becomes
//     the quorum of the schedule size MEASURED ON ENTRY into emergency, recorded in
//     dynamic_global_property_object::emergency_schedule_size_on_entry, floored at half the
//     maximum schedule (10 of 21). A chain that entered with 14 keyed validators can now leave
//     once 10 return, instead of never: the old constant asked for 15 of a schedule that could
//     not hold them, while the network's own quorum for 14 is 10.
//  2. The exit check runs BEFORE the hybrid schedule override. Until now the override padded the
//     schedule to 21 slots (committee filling the blanks) and only then did the exit fire, so for
//     up to 20 more blocks — until the next 21-block schedule rebuild — the chain demanded
//     quorum(21) = 15 signatures from at most R real signers (the producer of a certified block
//     does not sign it, and the committee account compensates that rather than adding slack).
//     With the check moved, the block after exit already uses the normal schedule the same block
//     built: R real validators, quorum(R).
//
// Decision: owner question #3396, option A. The threshold switch itself is
// emergency_exit_threshold_effective() in graphene/chain/emergency_exit.hpp — option B is that
// function's floor returning 0, option C keeps the legacy constant and does not call it.
//
// Activation: CHAIN_HARDFORK_17_TIME is a PLACEHOLDER. Nobody has announced this date; it must be
// set together with the release announcement, and it must stay in the future at that moment (the
// same warning as 14.hf/15.hf/16.hf: with a past date the fork activates in whatever block the
// 17th validator upgrades in, and there is no announceable moment). Building this branch already
// advertises version 4.3.0 — database.cpp _generate_block injects hardfork_version_vote while
// current_hardfork_version < CHAIN_HARDFORK_VERSION — so a binary built from it must not be
// deployed before the date is chosen.
//
// No state migration is needed at activation: emergency_schedule_size_on_entry defaults to 0,
// which the threshold reads as "not measured" and answers with the full-schedule quorum — i.e.
// exactly the legacy constant. An episode that started before this fork therefore still ends by
// the old rule; every later entry records its own size.
#ifndef CHAIN_HARDFORK_17
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_17 17
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_17_TIME 1798761600      // PLACEHOLDER 2027-01-01 00:00:00 UTC — NOT announced
#define CHAIN_HARDFORK_17_VERSION hardfork_version( version(4, 3, 0) )
#endif
